# Checkout bytes for a committed projection (ADR 0018). `req render --check` compares the file
# byte for byte with a freshly generated projection, and the generator writes LF. A Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true would otherwise rewrite docs/spec.md to CRLF and report it
# stale (exit 1) on a clean tree.
#
# Pinned per path rather than globally: `text=auto eol=lf` on every file would change how the
# corpus and the claims are checked out, which is a decision about the whole tree and not about
# the projection being compared.
docs/spec.md text eol=lf
# The CI snippet is compared **byte for byte** across three files (`tests/ci_template.rs`): a
# CRLF checkout would make the comparison fail on an unchanged tree, exactly as it would for the
# projection above. Pinned per path, for the same reason.
docs/adopting.md text eol=lf
examples/github-workflows/req.yml text eol=lf
